<h2>How to Know if Your Homeowners Insurance Covers a Detached Garage</h2>
<p>Determining if your homeowners insurance covers a detached garage involves a few steps:</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Review Your Insurance Policy:</strong> This is the first and most important step. Look for a section titled “Other Structures” or “Coverage B”. This <a href="https://www.floridapeninsula.com/homeowners-insurance/other-structures#:~:text=Coverage%20B%20will%20cover%20damage,of%20the%20Coverage%20A%20limit.">typically covers structures on your property that are not attached to your main home</a>, such as a detached garage.</li>
<li><strong>Check the Coverage Limits:</strong> Pay attention to the coverage limit for “Other Structures”. This is usually a percentage of the overall dwelling coverage, typically around 10%. For instance, if your house is insured for $200,000, your detached garage might be covered up to $20,000.</li>
<li><strong>Understand What’s Covered:</strong> Homeowners insurance generally covers certain perils like fire, theft, vandalism, and damage caused by vehicles. However, it may not cover all types of damage, like flooding or earthquakes. Make sure you understand what risks are covered.</li>
<li><strong>Consider the Contents:</strong> While the structure of your garage may be covered, the contents inside may require separate personal property coverage. If you store valuable items in your garage, you may need additional coverage.</li>
